0..73 Comment "//! Abstraction in rule terms [Gabbay-2009-nominal_universal_algebra] and"
74..153 Comment "//! [Fernandez-2007-nominal_rewriting]. At a port written `bind (a : N) . T`, a"
154..226 Comment "//! rule writes `bind a . t`: the atom `a` abstracted over the term `t`."
227..297 Comment "//! Admission re-mints every abstraction\'s atom by its depth among the"
298..373 Comment "//! abstractions above it, so `bind a . t` and `bind b . t` are one term to"
374..450 Comment "//! matching, the critical pairs and the kernel\'s replay alike. The value of"
451..527 Comment "//! `Theory` keeps each atom as written, as it keeps a rule\'s variables. The"
528..577 Comment "//! signature is `bind-port.gandr`\'s restriction."
578..581 Comment "//!"
582..634 Comment "//! - cites: [Gabbay-2009-nominal_universal_algebra]"
635..682 Comment "//! - cites: [Fernandez-2007-nominal_rewriting]"
683..686 Comment "//!"
687..863 Comment "//! [Gabbay-2009-nominal_universal_algebra]: https://doi.org/10.1093/logcom/exp033 \"Gabbay and Mathijssen, Nominal (Universal) Algebra: Equational Logic with Names and Binding\""
864..987 Comment "//! [Fernandez-2007-nominal_rewriting]: https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ic.2006.12.002 \"Fernández and Gabbay, Nominal rewriting\""
989..1063 Comment "/// Scope extrusion: a restriction over one side of a parallel composition"
1064..1137 Comment "/// encloses both. `q` moves under the restriction, so the law states `a`"
1138..1213 Comment "/// fresh for it (`freshness.gandr`). The checker orients the law, finds no"
1214..1267 Comment "/// critical pair and the kernel replays the verdict."
